{
 "command": "dialog-action-profiles",
 "notes": [
  "Feeds W8-18q (dialogs::action_profiles). Reflection over the internal ActionProfilesDialog and FileFilterText of the PhotoReview (Shell.Win32) assembly and the public ReviewAction / FileOperationType of PhotoReview.Core; no window is created. The language is the process default (English).",
  "Output per kind: dialog -> title, items [{class, id, text, style, ex_style}], initial_focus_id, default_button_id, resizable, header_ids, uses_modal_frame, extra_window_style; row_text -> text, badge (string or null); file_filter_parse -> filters [{name, pattern}]; preferred -> preferred_width, preferred_height, minimum_width, minimum_height; metrics -> margin, field_height, button_height, left_width; constants -> list_header_id ... apply_id.",
  "preferred and metrics use a window-less dialog (RuntimeHelpers.GetUninitializedObject with _avgCharWidth, _lineHeight, _childHosts set), so ButtonWidth is exactly Dx(50) and every measured height is 0. The wrapped-text heights of LayoutControls are hand-checked in the Rust tests with a fake measure.",
  "operation is the C# enum member name (Move, Copy, Recycle). The 'No key' action pins the badge rule (an empty shortcut gives a null badge); the 'Blank key' action pins that a blank shortcut still gives a badge (string.IsNullOrEmpty, not IsNullOrWhiteSpace)."
 ],
